course: dictionary
lesson: 8092
title: Reminders
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A reminder is a note, message or sign that helps you remember something. When you meet the word, read the words around it: they are its context, and they give you clues. «Keeping small reminders of good times, like notes or photos, can help on sad days.» Good times and photos tell you a reminder can be something that makes you think of the past.
explain: «Forgetting things is normal; a system such as a notes page or a reminder board on the fridge helps more than blaming yourself.» A board on the fridge helps you remember, so here a reminder is something that helps your memory. Some reminders are gentle too: «a gentle reminder» is a soft, kind way of saying "don't forget".
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. Does «a reminder board on the fridge helps» still make sense if you swap in "a note that helps you remember"? It does, so you have found the right meaning. Reminders can also be letters about bills, so check the clues each time.
fact: A reminder is a note, message or sign that helps you remember something.
fact: «Reminder» can also mean something that makes you think of a person, place or event from the past, like a photo.
fact: A reminder can be a letter telling you that something, like a bill, still has to be done or paid.
fact: Phrases to know: «set a reminder» (to remember later), «as a reminder» (to help you remember), «a reminder of» (something that brings back a memory).
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Forgetting things is normal; a reminder board on the fridge helps more than blaming yourself.» What is the reminder board for? | *To help you remember things | To draw pictures on the door | To keep the fridge cold | To blame people for forgetting
exercise: «Keeping small reminders of good times, like notes or photos, can help on sad days.» In this sentence, what does reminder mean? | A kind of food | A bill that must be paid | A loud alarm | *Something that makes you think of a happy past time
exercise: Your teacher writes, «Please bring your PE kit on Thursday, as a reminder.» What is the message for? | To sell you a new kit | *To help you remember your PE kit | To say you are very late | To tell you school is closed
test: Which one is a reminder? | A tall tree in the park | *A note that says "Trip on Friday"  | A note that says "Trip on Friday" | A loud song on the radio
test: A letter says your library book is still not returned, so you must pay. What is this letter? | A rainbow | A puzzle | *A reminder | A swimming hat
exam: Which word best means "something that helps you remember"? | Puzzle | Blanket | Stadium | *Reminder
